        "evidence": "There is one drawer (drawer:0#0,0#cut). A half base has a single cut face, and with that drawer fitted the configurator offers no other drawer spot. A full or quarter base takes no drawers at all."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "I couldn't build this as asked. One hex base holds one drawer at most, not five. Drawers only fit on the cut face of a half base. I tried a full base, which takes no drawers, and a quarter base, which also takes none. The half base takes exactly one. With that drawer fitted, the configurator offers no other drawer spot, even for drawers two storeys tall (I didn't try three-storey drawers after adding it). So the build is a single north-half hex base with one drawer in its cut face. The fit and collision checks passed. Since you asked for nothing beside or on top of it, I left out the usual end caps and joint bolts. That leaves three side edges without caps. More drawers would mean adding more bases, which goes against your brief.",
    "outcome": "compromise"
